==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Easter Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Easter Egg Cat''' when obtained from [[Eggy Cat Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Eggy Cat lacks any redeeming qualities as a generalist and is mostly ineffective against Angels due to his unreliable slow chance, brief slow duration, short attack range and single-target attacks. At most, he can be used as an inferior replacement to [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Toaster]] in some [[Restriction Stage]]s like [[Wrath of A-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of A-Cyclone]]. After clearing [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3, [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] can have his Target Angel [[Talents|Talent]] unlocked to become a much better alternative, as Sanzo has Area Attack and better stats overall. If no better units are owned, it is advised to at least evolve Eggy Cat into Easter Cat for the extra 100 range.

==='''True Form'''===
Easter Egg Cat is now guaranteed to slow Angels. This sets it apart from Sanzo, who has a considerably lower proc chance, making this unit more a reliable option when it comes to slowing enemies like [[Boraphim]] more consistently. However Easter Egg Cat's Single Attack, low range, and terrible survivability significantly affect its practical usage, as almost anything is capable of killing it instantly. This unit is better utilized over Sanzo or [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] in situations where peons control is largely irrelevant, and their superior range is not desired.

